%U A401103 3,3,9,7,5,0,9,3,1,6,9,3,4,2,4,4,6,9,8
%N A401103 Limit of A401100(n)/(5/2)^n.
%C A401103 In general, let {f_n}_{n>=0} be the sequence defined by f_{n+1} = alpha*f_n + e_n, where alpha > 1, a <= e_n <= b, then f_n = (f_0 + e_0/alpha + ... + e_{n-1}/alpha^n)*alpha^n = c*alpha^n - (e_n/alpha + e_{n+1}/alpha^2 + ...), where c = f_0 + Sum_{n>=0} e_n/alpha^{n+1}. We conclude that -(b/(alpha - 1))/alpha^n <= f_n/alpha^n - c <= -(a/(alpha - 1))/alpha^n.
%C A401103 Here we have alpha = 5/2, a = 0, and b = 1/2, so we have -(1/3)*(2/5)^n < A401100(n)/(5/2)^n - c < 0, since we have neither e_n = 0 for all sufficiently large n nor e_n = 1/2 for all sufficiently large n. [Corrected by _Alper Ferudun_ and _Jianing Song_, Oct 18 2026]
%H A401103 Jianing Song, <a href="/A401103/b401103.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1001</a>
%e A401103 1.2832560531219809208904351838894667247189...
%o A401103 (PARI) A401103(prec) = my(N = ceil(prec*log(10)/log(5/2)), A401100_N = 1); for(n=1, N, A401100_N = ceil(5*A401100_N/2)); [A401100_N/(5/2.)^N, (A401100_N+1/3)/(5/2.)^N] \\ outputs a lower bound and an upper bound that differ by at most (1/3)*10^(-prec), given sufficiently large realprecision
%Y A401103 Cf. A083286, A390321.
